00:02:27.450 --> 00:02:29.438
Now let's listen to a conversation.

45
00:02:29.738 --> 00:02:32.121
That influencer's photos must have been edited.

46
00:02:33.417 --> 00:02:36.371
They may well have been. Most images are filtered.

47
00:02:37.683 --> 00:02:40.298
It creates so much appearance pressure.

48
00:02:41.583 --> 00:02:47.022
Social comparison is dangerous for self-image. Could those ads have been designed to make us feel bad?

49
00:02:48.317 --> 00:02:51.538
Probably. That's how influencer marketing works.

50
00:02:52.850 --> 00:02:55.709
Choose role models who show authenticity, not perfection.

51
00:02:57.017 --> 00:02:59.771
Grammar focus: Modal perfect passive.

52
00:03:00.071 --> 00:03:05.391
Use a modal plus have been plus past participle to speculate about past passive actions.

53
00:03:05.691 --> 00:03:09.887
For example: The photo must have been edited. The video might have been deleted.

54
00:03:10.187 --> 00:03:12.918
It's useful when the action matters more than the person.

55
00:03:13.218 --> 00:03:17.389
Use this structure when you speculate about what was done to something, not who did it.

56
00:03:18.383 --> 00:03:20.862
Now read and listen. The Filter Effect.

57
00:03:21.162 --> 00:03:25.065
Many of the images we see online must have been edited before they were posted.

58
00:03:26.350 --> 00:03:29.801
Studies show that social comparison can lower our self-image.

59
00:03:31.117 --> 00:03:35.415
Influencer marketing often presents a perfect lifestyle that isn't real.

60
00:03:36.717 --> 00:03:40.760
However, more creators are now promoting authenticity and showing their real lives.

61
00:03:42.050 --> 00:03:45.396
Choosing positive role models can help reduce appearance pressure.

62
00:03:46.683 --> 00:03:49.057
Quiz time! Choose the correct answer.

63
00:03:49.357 --> 00:03:51.310
The way you see yourself is your blank.

64
00:03:51.610 --> 00:03:55.867
A, self-image. B, personal brand. C, role model.

65
00:03:59.883 --> 00:04:01.860
The answer is A: self-image.

66
00:04:03.350 --> 00:04:06.293
The door was open. It must blank by the cleaner.

67
00:04:06.593 --> 00:04:10.002
A, have opened. B, have been opened. C, been opened.

68
00:04:14.017 --> 00:04:15.947
The answer is B: have been opened.

69
00:04:17.450 --> 00:04:19.542
The message might blank to the wrong person.

70
00:04:19.842 --> 00:04:23.194
A, have been sent. B, have sent. C, be sending.

71
00:04:27.183 --> 00:04:28.997
The answer is A: have been sent.

72
00:04:30.483 --> 00:04:32.727
Being real and honest about who you are is blank.

73
00:04:33.027 --> 00:04:37.330
A, authenticity. B, beauty standards. C, social comparison.

74
00:04:41.317 --> 00:04:43.421
The answer is A: authenticity.

75
00:04:44.917 --> 00:04:47.996
According to the text, what can lower our self-image?

76
00:04:48.296 --> 00:04:52.286
A, authenticity. B, social comparison. C, role models.

77
00:04:56.283 --> 00:04:58.910
The answer is B: social comparison.

78
00:05:00.417 --> 00:05:05.217
Now it's your turn to speak. How does social media affect the way young people see themselves?

79
00:05:10.517 --> 00:05:17.627
Many photos must have been edited, so social comparison can damage self-image. Authentic role models help.

80
00:05:17.927 --> 00:05:19.393
Excellent answer, Nita!

81
00:05:20.383 --> 00:05:24.475
Great work today! You learned eight new words and modal perfect passive.

82
00:05:24.775 --> 00:05:28.577
Today's value is self-confidence. Believe in yourself.

83
00:05:28.877 --> 00:05:31.808
